Write a directive as `$name`. Some directives take an operand. For example,
`$before "Item: "` supplies a prefix. Separate head items with a comma.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    label = [$before "Item: ":[:Install]]
]

The child contributes `Install`. The parent adds its prefix to produce
`Item: Install`.

### Leave a comment with `$note`

Put a note inside a template body to leave a comment for the next reader.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    message = [:Build[$note: Version numbers go here later.] complete]
]

The result reads `Build complete`. The space before `complete` comes from the
outer body. The compiler skips the contents of the note.
